ond with the thematic knight maneuver ...Nd7–Nf8, reinforcing the kingside.} 10...Nd7 11.O-O-O {White castles long and dreams of delivering mate on our kingside. Our knight swings across for defense with 11...Nf8, but we will soon also launch our own attack.} 11...Nf8 12.Ng3 {White can try to attack the h5 pawn with 12.Ng3, but this leads nowhere. We defend solidly with 12...g6, reinforcing h5. Notice how the knight on f8 neatly prevents any Bxg6 tricks.} 12...g6 13.Ne4 {White continues maneuvering the knight forward, now targeting our f6 pawn.} 13...Be7 {We calmly defend with 13...Be7, securing f6. Now we’re ready to kick the knight out with ...f5, having stopped any Nf6 ideas, and follow up with the active ...Be6.} *

[Event "Chapter 5: The Classical Caro (3. Nc3/Nd2) Weapon 1: 4...Nf6! / Study 3: The Main Line 6. c3: White Castles Short or Long / Variation 10"]
