1.e4 {In this chapter, we will study the Two Knights, a solid system that White can play. We’ll focus on 3...Bg4, the solid main line, but with a slight twist of our own. You can find an alternative weapon against this system in the Bonus Lines course. As always, White starts with 1.e4, and we respond with the Caro-Kann: 1...c6.} 1...c6 2.Nc3 {White develops the knight to c3, reinforcing the center. We play 2...d5, as we always do in the Caro-Kann, challenging the center and building our Caro structure.} 2...d5 3.Nf3 {White develops the second knight to f3, entering the Two Knights Variation. It's played a quarter of the time. Our remedy against this solid setup is the main 3...Bg4, as mentioned in the introduction, bringing the bishop outside the pawn chain.} 3...Bg4 4.h3 {White’s best and most common reaction is to immediately question our bishop, a move played 42% of the time. We agree to trade and give up the bishop for the knight, since ...Bh5 could lead to dangerous g4 ideas. As a consequence, we’ll place all our pawns on light squares.} 4...Bxf3 5.Qxf3 {White recaptures with the queen, choosing not to damage their structure. As mentioned, we continue placing our pawns on light squares with 5...e6, compensating for the absence of our light-squared bishop.} 5...e6 6.Be2 {This bishop move, 6.Be2, is the main line at top-level play, even though it’s only played about 7% of the time below 2000 ELO. I’m a big fan of our solution here, a fianchetto approach. Most players aren’t aware of the best way to defend against it.} 6...g6 7.O-O {Most players in this position blindly castle, allowing us to place a powerful bishop on g7. So that’s exactly what we play, 7...Bg7.} 7...Bg7 8.Rd1 {White slides the rook to the d-file, trying to prepare d4. However, it’s too late, as we play ...d4 ourselves!} 8...d4 9.Nb1 {White is forced to retreat, so 9.Nb1 appears on the board.} 9...Ne7 {We continue development with 9...Ne7. Our plan is simple: castle short and support the d-pawn with ...c5, also freeing the c6 square for our b8-knight.} *

[Event "Chapter 6: The Two Knights (Nf3+Nc3): Weapon 1: 3...Bg4 / Study 1: The Solid 3...Bg4 / Variation 5"]
